From here, you can't see well what is going on in the savages' clearing, and coming closer is dangerous. Fortunately, Irene is with you.

"Irene, can you look what is going on there?"

"Easily!"

You didn't have time to reply before she disappeared into the thickets. After some time, the reeds finally move apart, and Irene returns.

"Henry, Henry, they've got Snoopy," she quietly gabbles, "he's in the cage, very close."

Carefully following Irene, you sneak closer to the clearing where the savages are dancing. So it is; Snoopy is sitting in the cage not far away.